      "message": "Doesn\u0027t need to be a member if you fetch this every time.\n\nI think there\u0027s some work TODO here to handle serialization as well; eg if app A asks for a bugreport, and then app B asks for it while dumpstate is still running, it would get the dumpstate service that is currently running for A. If that terminates when it\u0027s done with A, B would be left without a BR.\n\nYou might be able to deal with that in dumpstate itself, though maybe it\u0027s easier to just keep a queue of pending bugreports here, and then have a serialized loop something like this:\n1) Remove bugreport request from queue\n2) Start dumpstate with ctl.start\n3) Retrieve IDumpstate and register a death recipient on it\n4) Wait for the death recipient to fire (eg dumpstate has completed BR and exited)\n5) Goto 1\n\nFine to do in a follow-up CL.",
